1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,029
Orchard Core reads its settings from files, environment variables and the command line,

2
00:00:06,029 --> 00:00:08,787
and every tenant can add settings of its own.

3
00:00:08,787 --> 00:00:13,384
In this video, we'll see where configuration comes from, which source wins, and

4
00:00:13,384 --> 00:00:15,060
how to configure tenants.

5
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:23,799
ASP.NET Core has one configuration for the whole application.

6
00:00:23,799 --> 00:00:30,348
Orchard Core adds IShellConfiguration, which extends IConfiguration, so each tenant reads the shared

7
00:00:30,348 --> 00:00:33,560
settings with its own settings layered on top.

8
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:39,741
All the configuration of Orchard Core sits under one section named OrchardCore.

9
00:00:39,741 --> 00:00:42,616
Modules nest their settings by service:

10
00:00:42,616 --> 00:00:47,343
the Azure settings of the Media module are in Media, then Azure, and

11
00:00:47,343 --> 00:00:50,410
the SMTP settings are in Email, then Smtp.

12
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:54,875
Section names carry no OrchardCore underscore prefix.

13
00:00:54,875 --> 00:01:00,480
Deprecated names such as OrchardCore_Media_Azure are read as well, and when a value

14
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:03,818
is set under both names, the current name wins.

15
00:01:03,818 --> 00:01:08,100
An array under the current name replaces the deprecated array.

16
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:13,467
Only modules that read a section are configured by it, so check the

17
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:16,566
documentation of a module for its settings.

18
00:01:16,566 --> 00:01:22,890
The appsettings.json file of the Orchard Core CMS web project lists many sections as comments.

19
00:01:27,090 --> 00:01:30,505
Environment variables follow the same paths.

20
00:01:30,505 --> 00:01:37,883
A double underscore replaces each colon, so OrchardCore__Media__MaxFileSize sets the maximum file size

21
00:01:37,883 --> 00:01:40,820
of the Media module for every tenant.

22
00:01:41,570 --> 00:01:47,016
Put a tenant name right after OrchardCore, and the value applies to that tenant only:

23
00:01:47,016 --> 00:01:49,829
Default, or the name of any other tenant.

24
00:01:49,829 --> 00:01:54,438
A tenant's value wins over the shared one, except for settings the host

25
00:01:54,438 --> 00:01:57,550
reads for all tenants, like BackgroundService.

26
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:01,333
Hosting platforms use the same variables:

27
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:07,141
Azure App Settings reach the site as environment variables, on Windows and on Linux.

28
00:02:07,141 --> 00:02:13,400
A pipeline can also transform the appsettings.json file with values from its own variables.

29
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:23,855
ASP.NET Core loads appsettings.json first, then the file of the current environment, such

30
00:02:23,855 --> 00:02:29,650
as appsettings.Development.json, then user secrets in the Development environment.

31
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:35,425
Next, Orchard Core adds the appsettings.json file of the App_Data folder, then the

32
00:02:35,425 --> 00:02:39,765
file of the current environment, such as appsettings.Development.json.

33
00:02:39,765 --> 00:02:42,620
They override the files of the host project.

34
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:47,102
Environment variables and command-line arguments come after.

35
00:02:47,102 --> 00:02:51,964
ASP.NET Core loads them before the App_Data files, and Orchard Core applies them

36
00:02:51,964 --> 00:02:55,470
again at this point, so they win over every file so far.

37
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:58,767
Last come the settings of the tenant:

38
00:02:58,767 --> 00:03:04,809
its own section under OrchardCore, then the appsettings.json file in its own folder of App_Data.

39
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:08,600
A later source wins, so a tenant value beats a shared one.

40
00:03:09,350 --> 00:03:13,129
By default the App_Data folder sits in the application folder.

41
00:03:13,129 --> 00:03:18,241
The ORCHARD_APP_DATA environment variable moves it, to a relative or an absolute path,

42
00:03:18,241 --> 00:03:21,520
and Orchard Core creates the folder if it is missing.

43
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:29,929
To configure a tenant before it exists, add a section named for the

44
00:03:29,929 --> 00:03:33,504
tenant under OrchardCore, with a State of Uninitialized.

45
00:03:33,504 --> 00:03:38,174
Its URL prefix routes requests to the tenant, and its database provider and

46
00:03:38,174 --> 00:03:40,480
recipe are used when it is set up.

47
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:46,653
Orchard Core treats any section under OrchardCore that has a valid State as a tenant.

48
00:03:46,653 --> 00:03:51,123
A section without a State only adds configuration, as we'll see for a

49
00:03:51,123 --> 00:03:53,090
tenant that already exists.

50
00:03:54,744 --> 00:04:00,714
With the Tenants feature enabled, the list under Multi-Tenancy, Tenants shows MyTenant, although

51
00:04:00,714 --> 00:04:02,470
nobody created it there.

52
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:05,103
Its badges come from the configuration:

53
00:04:05,103 --> 00:04:09,844
the Sqlite database provider, the SaaS recipe, and the state Uninitialized.

54
00:04:10,316 --> 00:04:12,730
Setup opens the tenant's own address.

55
00:04:12,730 --> 00:04:16,547
The screen asks for the site name, the time zone and the Super

56
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:21,936
User, but not for a recipe or a database, because the configuration already provides them.

57
00:04:23,536 --> 00:04:29,081
Once a tenant exists, a section with its name, and no State, sets its configuration.

58
00:04:29,081 --> 00:04:34,626
This one sets the maximum file size of the Media module for the Default tenant only.

59
00:04:35,376 --> 00:04:40,508
A tenant section shares its path with the module sections under OrchardCore.

60
00:04:40,508 --> 00:04:45,076
Never name a tenant after a module section, such as Media or Email.

61
00:04:45,826 --> 00:04:51,650
Each tenant can also have its own appsettings.json file, in a folder named for the tenant.

62
00:04:51,650 --> 00:04:56,199
Its keys sit at the root, without an OrchardCore section, and no file

63
00:04:56,199 --> 00:04:58,686
for a specific environment is read.

64
00:04:59,436 --> 00:05:04,156
Orchard Core writes this file during setup, and keeps only the values that

65
00:05:04,156 --> 00:05:06,988
differ from the application configuration.

66
00:05:06,988 --> 00:05:11,412
The State and the URL of the tenant are saved apart, in tenants.json,

67
00:05:11,412 --> 00:05:12,946
under the same rule.

68
00:05:17,146 --> 00:05:22,687
To give every tenant the same database, set the DatabaseProvider and the ConnectionString

69
00:05:22,687 --> 00:05:25,661
once, at the root of the OrchardCore section.

70
00:05:25,661 --> 00:05:31,376
A Default section can give the Default tenant its own TablePrefix, keeping its tables apart.

71
00:05:32,126 --> 00:05:38,437
Under Tenants, TablePrefixPattern and SchemaPattern generate the table prefix and schema of each

72
00:05:38,437 --> 00:05:43,757
tenant created in the admin or the API, from a template such as the tenant name.

73
00:05:43,757 --> 00:05:49,696
The values must be valid SQL identifiers, and RequireTablePrefix makes a prefix mandatory.

74
00:05:50,446 --> 00:05:54,715
These settings apply to SQL Server, MySQL and PostgreSQL.

75
00:05:54,715 --> 00:05:58,442
SQLite does not use the shared connection string:

76
00:05:58,442 --> 00:06:01,626
it keeps a database file for each tenant.

77
00:06:05,826 --> 00:06:12,001
In your own module, a Startup class receives IShellConfiguration, and binds a section

78
00:06:12,001 --> 00:06:13,765
to an options class.

79
00:06:13,765 --> 00:06:20,346
The Tenants module binds Tenants, and also accepts the deprecated name OrchardCore_Tenants.

80
00:06:21,096 --> 00:06:27,460
For your own sections, skip the prefix and nest by service, such as MyService and MyProvider.

81
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:30,866
The environment variable names then stay short.

82
00:06:31,616 --> 00:06:34,393
A module can also describe its sections.

83
00:06:34,393 --> 00:06:39,945
Ship a ConfigurationSchema.json file in the package, with a targets file that declares

84
00:06:39,945 --> 00:06:45,196
it, and Visual Studio suggests and validates those settings in appsettings files.

85
00:06:47,196 --> 00:06:49,614
That's configuration in Orchard Core:

86
00:06:49,614 --> 00:06:55,235
sections under OrchardCore, files and environment variables, and tenant values layered on top.

87
00:06:55,235 --> 00:06:56,696
Thanks for watching.

